{
  "_comment": [
    "sg13cmos5l-bandgap -- operating-point attribution for the FAILED `psrr_dc` row of",
    "spec/target-spec.md (issue #93). This bench GRADES NOTHING: it carries no `limits` and no",
    "`spec_row` tag, is cited by no manifest item, and adds no coverage claim. It exists to say WHY",
    "the committed sim/closed-loop-psrr grid misses its ratified Target, which that grid records but",
    "does not explain. The ratified bound is untouched.",
    "",
    "SUB-GRID, not the full 45: process {typ, wcs} x supply {2.970, 3.300, 3.630} V x {27, 125} C =",
    "12 points. It is a cross product because `corners` is one, and it is THIS cross product because",
    "the question is the supply dependence: each (process, temperature) pair appears at all three",
    "supplies, so within each such triple vdd is the only thing that moves. It contains the",
    "three points the issue requires -- the worst failing point wcs/2.970V/125C (55.249 dB in the",
    "committed grid), a passing 3.63 V point (all four 3.63 V points pass; wcs/3.630V/125C is",
    "67.470 dB), and typ/3.300V/27C (59.443 dB) -- and 6 of the 12 fail the Target in that grid,",
    "6 pass.",
    "",
    "THREE SOLVES PER POINT, all DC `op`. No `ac` analysis and no frequency point: the row is DC",
    "only (sim/closed-loop-psrr/README.md says why), and no loop-break deck is used.",
    "  - `lo` and `hi` are the committed PSRR bench's own two solves, in the same order with the",
    "    same +/-0.05 V `Vpsrr` alters, so psrr_db here is the same secant and must reproduce the",
    "    committed grid's value at the same point (the bench README quotes both numbers).",
    "  - `op` returns `Vpsrr` to its deck default of 0 V. A 0 V source is a DC short, so this third",
    "    solve is the UNPERTURBED bias the secant was taken about -- the right operating point to",
    "    attribute the miss to. The steps are cumulative (no `reset`), so it starts from `hi`'s",
    "    solution and converges to the unperturbed point.",
    "",
    "WHY THE DEVICE PARAMETERS ARE WRITTEN BY HAND AS `@n....` EXPRESSIONS. `klt sim --op-lint`",
    "is the obvious instrument and cannot do this on SG13CMOS5L: the PDK's `.subckt sg13_hv_pmos`",
    "wraps an OSDI (PSP103) `N` instance, the lint probes only `@m.<path>.<element>`, and the",
    "`op_lint.models.*.op_point_element` override substitutes the element name but not the `@m.`",
    "prefix -- so every value comes back null with `region: \"unknown\"`. Filed as generic tool",
    "friction at 2AMLogic/klayout-tools#5637; this bench does not wait on it. The expressions below",
    "lower into the same `.control` `let`/`print` idiom klt uses for any `measurements[].expr`.",
    "",
    "THERE IS NO `vdsat` ON THIS PDK. PSP103 exposes `vdss`, its own name for the saturation",
    "voltage; `save @n....[vdsat]` fails with 'vector is not available'. So the issue's",
    "`vds - vdsat` margin is recorded here as `<dev>_marg_v = |vds| - |vdss|`, over all 14 MOS",
    "devices. The magnitudes are taken because PSP103 reports device-oriented quantities, so the",
    "expression is correct for both the p- and the n-channel devices without a per-type sign rule.",
    "A negative margin is a device out of saturation and is RECORDED AS SUCH -- it is not graded,",
    "not clamped and not dropped.",
    "",
    "TWO FIGURES ABOUT THE AMPLIFIER, one of which is deliberately NOT a gain. The issue asks for",
    "'the amplifier's DC gain or an equivalent loop-gain figure':",
    "  - `av_amp_derived` is the DC GAIN FIGURE the issue asks for. It is DERIVED from the",
    "    measured op point by the textbook two-stage",
    "    small-signal formula, 0.5 * av1 * gm2_s * rout_ohm, with av1, gm2_s and rout_ohm recorded",
    "    separately so the arithmetic can be re-done from the raw gm/gds. Its stated neglects: the",
    "    body effect (gmb), and the tail-current feedback from xmtail's gate being the amplifier's",
    "    own output node fb.",
    "  - `fb_per_dvid` is MEASURED and is NOT a gain: it is |d(fb)/d(sns2-sns1)| across the supply",
    "    secant, i.e. the gain the feedback loop WOULD need if the differential input error were the",
    "    only thing moving fb. The rail also moves the amplifier's own supply-referred bias (xmtail,",
    "    xmp3 and xmp4 have their sources on vdd), so it is not. Recorded precisely because",
    "    comparing it with `av_amp_derived` measures how much of fb's tracking the loop cannot",
    "    account for.",
    "Every per-device gm, gds, ids, vgs, vds and vdss is recorded, so any other figure a reader",
    "prefers can be recomputed from the record without re-running the bench.",
    "",
    "THE MIRROR LEG IS TESTED, NOT ASSERTED. `dids_m3_a` is the measured change in the output",
    "mirror leg's current across the secant; `dids_m3_predicted_a` is what the measured small-signal",
    "parameters predict for it, gm3*(dvdd - dfb) + gds3*(dvdd - dvref) in PSP103's device-oriented",
    "convention. Agreement means the mirror's own channel-length modulation plus the imperfect",
    "tracking of fb accounts for the whole error; a gap means something else does. The two terms are",
    "also recorded SEPARATELY (`dids_m3_gds_term_a`, `dids_m3_gm_term_a`) because they have opposite",
    "signs and nearly cancel, so the sum alone would hide which one is large. `rbranch_ohm` is the",
    "measured d(vref)/d(ids_m3) of the output branch (XR1 in series with XQ3's own slope), the gain",
    "that turns that residual current into the recorded d(vref). `r1_ohm` and `r2_ohm` measure the",
    "two core resistors themselves from the op point ((vref - e3)/ids_m3 and (sns2 - e2)/ids_m2),",
    "so rbranch_ohm's composition is measured rather than attributed to XR1 by its geometry.",
    "",
    "THE STARTUP LEG IS INCLUDED SO IT CAN BE RULED OUT BY MEASUREMENT. xx3.xmkfb pulls fb toward",
    "vss and would be a competing, supply-dependent mechanism independent of any headroom; its ids",
    "and vds, and the det node it is gated from, are recorded at every point.",
    "",
    "PORTABLE BY CONSTRUCTION, on the same terms as the five grid benches: `models.pdk` plus",
    "PDK-relative per-section corner libraries (no absolute host path, which `batch` refuses),",
    "`$PDK_ROOT/...` osdi_preload entries the runner resolves on its own box, and",
    "`options.stage_model_inputs: true` so the model text behind every figure is bound to",
    "sim/pdk.json's pin by sha256. `netlist` is the deck sim/grid-run.sh generates under sim/build/",
    "(gitignored). The solver tolerances and `numdgt`/`measureprec` are the PSRR bench's, unchanged,",
    "so the secant is the same numerical object.",
    "",
    "THE PER-DEVICE MEASUREMENT BLOCK IS MACHINE-GENERATED (14 devices x 6 quantities is too long",
    "to hand-write without a transcription error), from a one-shot script that is not part of the",
    "bench. THIS FILE is the committed artifact and the thing that runs; the record's",
    "request_sha256 binds it.",
    "",
    "Process labels map to model sections exactly as spec/target-spec.md \u00a7PVT does.",
    "`netlist_source` is `schematic`: the DUT is the decision-record-0006 migrated xschem export."
  ],
